  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q24-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Bag 1 has one ball labelled 1. Bag 2 has balls labelled 1 and 2. Bag 3 has balls labelled 1, 2, and 3. A bag is chosen at random, and then a ball is drawn. Given that the ball is labelled 1, find the probability it came from Bag 1.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{6}{11}$.\n\nDivide the probability of choosing Bag 1 and drawing 1 by the total probability of drawing 1.",
      "worked": "Let $B_i$ denote choosing Bag $i$, and let $L$ denote drawing a ball labelled 1. Each bag is chosen with probability $\\frac13$. The conditional probabilities of drawing 1 from Bags 1, 2 and 3 are $1$, $\\frac12$ and $\\frac13$, respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(B_1\\cap L)&=\\frac13\\times1=\\frac13.\\\\\\Pr(L)&=\\frac13\\times1+\\frac13\\times\\frac12+\\frac13\\times\\frac13\\\\\\Pr(L)&=\\frac13+\\frac16+\\frac19=\\frac{11}{18}.\\\\\\Pr(B_1\\mid L)&=\\frac{\\Pr(B_1\\cap L)}{\\Pr(L)}\\\\\\Pr(B_1\\mid L)&=\\frac{1/3}{11/18}=\\frac6{11}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
